CONTEXT
    # Pull Request

    ## Title

    <TICKET-ID>: <Capitalized action summary>

    ## Description

    Branch name:
    `<branch-name>`

    Implementation Summary:

    - Fix / implementation: <short paragraph: what now happens when the user acts, a brief example when useful, then how the app makes it happen; simple sentences in event order>
    - Root cause: <short paragraph: what the app did before, the missing or incorrect action, and the problem the user saw; simple sentences in event order, or None>

    Code Layer Impact:

    - Impacted services: <repository names without owner/organization prefixes, or None>
    - Core modules/sections: <affected modules or sections>

    UI Impact:

    - New/updated components, layouts, or pages: <affected UI or None>

    DB Impact:

    - New/updated tables: <affected tables or None>
    - Indexing added/updated: <affected indexes or None>

    Infra Impact:

    - Env changes: <environment changes or None>
    - Cloudflare/S3/Redis or other infra changes: <infrastructure changes or None>
AS pr_template

USE ../knowledge/summary-knowledge.flow
USE ../knowledge/common-knowledge.flow
USE ../knowledge/draft-knowledge.flow
USE pr-git-rules.flow

DO Resolve the explicit project or current checkout and active ticket from
    @request or conversation. Reject supplied-ID mismatches. Return an object
    with project, ticket_id (NULL if unknown), and ticket (complete matching
    cached Jira object or NULL). AS task_context

IF @task_context.ticket_id == NULL
    ASK "Which Jira ticket should this work use?" AS ticket_input
    DO Validate @ticket_input against the active task and return @task_context
        updated with that one Jira ID. AS task_context

SET project = @task_context.project
SET ticket_id = @task_context.ticket_id
SET ticket = @task_context.ticket

DO Retain the verified project, ticket ID, and any complete cached ticket as
    this conversation's active task without remote calls or task files.

DO Resolve and read the pr.md draft for @project and @ticket_id under
    @draft_rules. Allow a new draft only when none is known.
    Return an object with path and text (both NULL for a new draft). AS draft_state

SET draft_path = @draft_state.path
SET saved_draft = @draft_state.text

DO Read applicable project AGENTS.md and explicit user naming overrides.
    Current rules take precedence over old conversation conventions. AS project_rules

IF @ticket == NULL
    USE ../knowledge/tool-knowledge.flow
    DO Resolve private absolute acli using @tool_guidance. Return its path. AS acli
    RUN @acli jira workitem view @ticket_id --fields "key,issuetype,summary,status,assignee,description,attachment" --json
    AS ticket_result
    DO Parse @ticket_result.stdout as JSON, verify its key equals @ticket_id and
        requested details are complete, and retain the full ticket and project.
        Return the complete object. AS ticket

PRINT """
- [ ] Git validation
- [ ] Evidence/verification
- [ ] Save/publication
"""

DO Read @request and prior explicit choices for this PR. Return the explicitly
    selected target branch, including a target-only request, or NULL. Never
    infer a target from defaults or existing PRs. AS target

IF @target == NULL
    ASK "Which destination branch should this PR target?" AS target

IF @target == ""
    RETURN "PR preparation requires an explicitly selected destination branch."

DO Validate @project for explicit @target and @ticket_id under @git_rules and
    @project_rules. Inspect branch, HEAD, remotes, full status, and Git operation
    state; fetch the selected target and resolve its exact revision and merge base.
    Return an object with current_branch, checked_head, repository, push_remote,
    target_remote, target_ref, target_revision, merge_base, and commit_range
    containing the literal target_ref..HEAD range. AS git_state

RUN git -C @project log --reverse "--format=%H%n%B%x00" @git_state.commit_range
AS commits_result

DO Parse every SHA and full message from @commits_result.stdout, including merges.
    Preserve whitespace except separators and one terminal newline. Verify the
    nonempty range and all messages against @git_rules and @project_rules for
    @ticket_id. Return ordered messages and SHAs. AS checked_messages

PRINT """
- [x] Git validation
- [ ] Evidence/verification
- [ ] Save/publication
"""

DO Use @ticket and @saved_draft. Return an object with the complete ticket,
    saved_pr (NULL for a new draft), and unrequested PR sections to preserve. AS documents

RUN git -C @project diff --find-renames @git_state.merge_base @git_state.checked_head
AS diff_result

DO Review @diff_result.stdout and relevant code read-only. Verify
    @checked_messages against implementation evidence. Follow exact imports or
    symbols into direct dependencies only for material gaps and stop once claims
    are supported. Return an object with evidence, material_concerns, and
    observed_checks. Intent and messages are not implementation proof. AS review

DO Compose an in-memory PR draft from @documents, @review, @writing_guidance,
    @summary_rules, and @pr_template. Preserve accurate developer notes, labels,
    order, and unrequested sections. Default the title to one concise
    <TICKET-ID>: <Capitalized action summary> line unless explicitly overridden.
    Return only the completed draft. AS draft

DO Run only missing project-required checks for the current code and inputs,
    reusing unchanged observed results. Inspect one targeted manifest or
    Makefile only when needed. Probe runtime health only after an actual failure.
    Retain every exit and never mask failures. Return the verification results. AS verification

DO Verify @review has no unresolved material correctness concern, @verification
    passed all required checks, @checked_messages and @draft are accurate, and
    the ticket work is complete.

PRINT """
- [x] Git validation
- [x] Evidence/verification
- [ ] Save/publication
"""

DO Immediately re-read branch, HEAD, @git_state.target_ref revision, active task context, Git
    operation state, and the full index and tree. Revalidate only changed
    dependencies. Verify they still match @git_state.checked_head, @git_state.target_revision,
    @ticket_id, @review, and @verification. AS final_gate

DO Save @draft to the PR draft under @draft_rules, using @draft_path when
    present and @saved_draft as the concurrent-edit baseline. For a new file
    allocate only its unique external temporary directory. Return the absolute
    saved path without pushing or publishing. AS draft_path

PRINT """
- [x] Git validation
- [x] Evidence/verification
- [x] Save/publication
"""

PRINT Report @draft_path, @review.observed_checks, blockers, gaps, and partial success briefly.
